<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>NYT &gt; Technology</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/section/technology</link><description>Technology industry news, commentary, and analysis, with reporting on big tech, startups, and internet culture. The New York Times is a hub for conversation about news and ideas.</description><atom:link rel="self" href="https://rss.nytimes.com/services/xml/rss/nyt/Technology.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><item><title>Follow the Markets and Track Stocks With These Free Apps</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/06/technology/personaltech/finance-stocks-apps.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/06/technology/personaltech/finance-stocks-apps.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/06/technology/personaltech/finance-stocks-apps.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>Google Finance and Apple’s Stocks app have added new features over the years to make them more useful for tracking the markets and your investments.</description><dc:creator>J. D. Biersdorfer</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 09:03:19 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Mobile Apps</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">None</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Android</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Apple</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Google</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Stocks</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Bonds</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Personal finance</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/08/05/technology/personaltech/05BIZ-TECHTIP-TOPART/05BIZ-TECHTIP-TOPART-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Apple</media:credit><media:description>Apple's free Stocks app for its devices provides a dashboard for following personal investments, markets and financial news.</media:description></media:content></item><item><title>Laptop Fire on American Airlines Flight Injures at Least One Passenger</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/24/travel/american-airlines-laptop-fire.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/24/travel/american-airlines-laptop-fire.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/24/travel/american-airlines-laptop-fire.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>Flight attendants used a fireproof bag to contain the computer after its lithium battery began smoking. One passenger was treated on the ground for injuries.</description><dc:creator>Christine Chung</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 19:34:57 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Airlines</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">airplanes</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Travel</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Tourism</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">vacations</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Fires</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Plane Crash</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Laptop</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Batteries</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Lithium Mental</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">American Airlines</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Atlanta</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Dallas</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Fort Worth TX</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/08/24/multimedia/24trav-laptopfire-jgkp/24trav-laptopfire-jgkp-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Caroline Brehman/EPA, via Shutterstock</media:credit><media:description>Flight attendants acted quickly to stop a laptop fire on Friday evening aboard an American Airlines flight from Atlanta to Dallas-Fort Worth. </media:description></media:content></item><item><title>OpenAI’s Two-Week Pause + Jill Lepore on the Threat of the “Artificial State” + Train of Thought</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/21/podcasts/openais-two-week-pause-jill-lepore-on-the-threat-of-the-artificial-state-train-of-thought.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/21/podcasts/openais-two-week-pause-jill-lepore-on-the-threat-of-the-artificial-state-train-of-thought.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/21/podcasts/openais-two-week-pause-jill-lepore-on-the-threat-of-the-artificial-state-train-of-thought.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>“It is the first time that we know of that a major lab has voluntarily slowed down.”</description><dc:creator>Kevin Roose, Casey Newton, Whitney Jones, Rachel Cohn, Vjeran Pavic, Katie McMurran, Dan Powell, Marion Lozano, Rowan Niemisto and Alyssa Moxley</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 11:00:03 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">science</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.c